# Architecture Knowledge

## Shape

A modular monolith: one deployable NestJS app, split into business modules with hard boundaries,
so any module can later be extracted without untangling imports.

```
src/
  main.ts
  app.module.ts
  config/                 env schema (zod), AppConfig, AppConfigModule
  common/
    errors/               ErrorCode enum, AppException, error envelope types
    filters/              AllExceptionsFilter
    guards/               JwtAuthGuard, PermissionGuard, CsrfGuard, ThrottlerGuard wiring
    decorators/           @Public(), @RequirePermission(), @CurrentUser()
    interceptors/         request id, logging context
    pagination/           PaginationQueryDto, paginated() helper, Paginated<T>
    i18n/                 locale resolution from X-Locale, message catalogues
    utils/
  infrastructure/
    database/             PrismaService | TypeORM DataSource, transaction helper, migrations
    mail/                 MailService, SMTP transport, templates
    storage/              StoragePort + s3 / local adapters
    outbox/               outbox table, dispatcher worker
  modules/
    auth/
    users/
    <domain>/
test/
  helpers/                app factory, db reset, auth helper, mail sink reader
  <domain>/*.e2e-spec.ts
```

## Dependency direction

```
config  ←  common  ←  infrastructure  ←  modules
```

An arrow points at what may be imported. `common` never imports `infrastructure` or `modules`;
`infrastructure` never imports `modules`. Enforced by the `no-restricted-imports` layer rules in
`eslint.config.mjs`.

## A module

```
modules/users/
  users.module.ts
  users.controller.ts          HTTP
  users.service.ts             business rules
  users.repository.ts          ORM access
  users.mapper.ts              entity → response DTO
  dto/
    create-user.dto.ts
    update-user.dto.ts
    user-response.dto.ts
    list-users-query.dto.ts
  users.types.ts               domain types, status unions
  users.service.spec.ts
  index.ts                     public API: the module and the exported service/types
```

Other modules import `@/modules/users` (the `index.ts`) and nothing deeper.

### Layers

| Layer | May | May not |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Controller | route, guards, `@Body()`/`@Query()` DTOs, call **one** service method, map response | business rules, ORM, try/catch that swallows errors |
| Service | rules, ownership checks, transactions, call repositories and other modules' services, enqueue outbox events | know about `Request`/`Response`, cookies, HTTP status codes other than via `AppException` |
| Repository | ORM queries, return domain types | business decisions, throwing HTTP-flavoured errors except `NOT_FOUND` mapping when agreed |
| Mapper | pure functions entity → DTO | I/O |

### Cross-module calls

- Call the other module's **exported service**. Never its repository.
- Need data from two modules in one transaction → the transaction is started by the calling
  service and passed down (see `07-database-*.mdc` → Transactions).
- Reacting to something another module did → an outbox/domain event, not a direct call back.
- A cycle between two modules means one of them owns something it should not. Move it; do not
  `forwardRef`.

## What goes where

| Thing | Location |
| --- | --- |
| New business capability | `modules/<domain>` |
| Talking to an external system (SMTP, S3, payment provider, third-party API) | `infrastructure/<system>` behind an interface |
| Something every module uses and that has no business meaning | `common/` |
| Env var | `config/env.schema.ts` + `AppConfig` |

## Rules

- No new top-level folders.
- No generic `BaseService` / `BaseRepository` unless one already exists.
- One module per business domain, not per table.
- Controllers stay thin enough that an e2e test is the only test they need.
